  "readmeFile": "ReadmeNuget.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- Bulk import: submissions that consist only of new records (e.g. CSV import from scripts) can now be executed as multi-row bulk INSERTs, greatly reducing the time of large imports. Set ModuleDataIO.BulkAddThreshold to enable (disabled by default); only submissions that declare AllowBulkInsert and are safe to batch (single module, pure adds, no per-row SQL hooks) take the bulk path, everything else keeps the row-by-row behavior.\n- Script engine: types that take a module as a generic type argument (the ModuleSearcher<TModule> idiom) are now extensible. A registered type with a constructor (string moduleDesignName) can be written as new Xxx<SomeModule>() in scripts, and completion resolves its Module / ModuleData members to that module's type, so packages can provide their own module-generic script objects.\n- DateField: in year/month-only mode the read-only display now uses a year-month format when no explicit Format is specified, matching the month editor.\n- ListField: the detail / delete command buttons are now vertically centered in rows.\n- FileField: the upload button is now shown as disabled (dimmed, no hover feedback) while the field is disabled.\n- Module design files: saving no longer writes the runtime SQL buffers (QueryField QueryText / ExecuteSqlField SqlText) or the auto-generated link fields into *.mod.json - the *.sql files remain the single source of truth. This fixes stale SQL appearing in the JSON of a copied module and link-field definitions being baked in when a module is renamed.",
